Import `math` and document the module as providing small numeric helpers for a report generator.

## add
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus zero times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## sub
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## mul
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twice `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## div
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus three times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## mod
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus four times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## pow
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus five times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## min
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus six times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## max
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus seven times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## mean
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus eight times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## median
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus nine times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## clamp
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus ten times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## lerp
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus eleven times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## sign
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twelve times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## abs_diff
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus thirteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## is_even
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus fourteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## is_odd
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus fifteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## gcd
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus sixteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## lcm
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus seventeen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## fact
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus eighteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## fib
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus nineteen times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## sum_sq
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twenty times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## norm
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twenty-one times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## dot
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twenty-two times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## dist
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twenty-three times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

## argmax
Require `a` to be non-`None`, then return `a` plus twenty-four times `b`; use `1` as the default for `b`.

